  "result": "It needs changes before publishing \u2014 two issues stand out:\n\n1. **\"Fully compliant with the framework\"** is risky. NIST SP 800-61 is guidance, not a certifiable standard with a pass/fail checklist, so \"fully compliant\" is a strong, hard-to-substantiate claim that could bite you if a customer relies on it for their own compliance/audit purposes. Safer phrasing: \"follows the guidance in NIST SP 800-61\" or \"aligns with the NIST SP 800-61 framework.\"\n\n2. **The uncited conference talk** shouldn't go out as-is. Publishing \"we drew inspiration from something but can't cite it\" is both unprofessional-looking and a potential attribution problem if you used specific concepts/frameworks from that talk. Either track down the speaker/talk and cite it properly, or drop the reference entirely and just describe the SRE practices you incorporated in your own words.",
